Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||08-30-2000||02:03 PM||||Ok since when does 19,700 Miles = "original miles unknown, maybe less than 120,000."  Something really fishy here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>It's probably been fully restored, it looks nice, but I'd want to hear it run before I threw any money at it.<P>I'm not fond of people who are not upfront on miles, if it has 19,700 miles on it since it was restored, ok, but I don't want to find out that's not the case reading further on.  I would pass on the whole car just for that reason.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||13
Z||000002||Oreif||08-30-2000||02:23 PM||||It sounds like they are selling it on consignment. I bet they don't know the odometer goes out 6 digits. I would guess the car really has 19,700 miles but they probably don't think a car that old can have 19K on so they are assuming the odometer rolled over. I know some states after a certain year print the title's as "Mileage Unknown" Nice looking car. If I were a bidder I'd want to examine the car before bidding.||||reg||1
